  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Peter",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 5,
    "summary": "The elders are to feed the flock of God—Humility and godly graces lead to perfection.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The elders which are among you I exhort, who am also an elder, and a witness of the sufferings of Christ, and also a partaker of the glory that shall be revealed:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "TG Elder, Melchizedek Priesthood; Leadership."
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "D&C 66:2; 93:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Feed the flock of God which is among you, taking the oversight thereof, not by constraint, but willingly; not for filthy lucre, but of a ready mind;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "GR Tend, Superintend. John 21:16 (15–16)."
          },
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "GR overseeing, guarding, watching."
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "TG Initiative."
          },
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "TG Filthiness."
          },
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 126,
            "text": "TG Priestcraft."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither as being lords over God’s heritage, but being ensamples to the flock.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "D&C 121:41 (41–42)."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Example."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And when the chief Shepherd shall appear, ye shall receive a crown of glory that fadeth not away.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Good Shepherd; Shepherd."
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "Luke 12:44. TG Exaltation."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "D&C 66:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Likewise, ye younger, submit yourselves unto the elder. Yea, all of you be subject one to another, and be clothed with humility: for God resisteth the proud, and giveth grace to the humble.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Respect; Submissiveness."
          },
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 127,
            "text": "TG Humility."
          },
          {
            "start": 137,
            "end": 146,
            "text": "GR opposes, is adverse to."
          },
          {
            "start": 151,
            "end": 156,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          },
          {
            "start": 182,
            "end": 188,
            "text": "TG Poor in Spirit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Contrite Heart."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Levity."
          },
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Watch."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Devil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whom resist steadfast in the faith, knowing that the same afflictions are accomplished in your brethren that are in the world.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG Perseverance; Steadfastness."
          },
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "GR laid upon, endured by."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But the God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after that ye have suffered a while, make you perfect, stablish, strengthen, settle you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "TG Worthiness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 169,
            "end": 173
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To him be glory and dominion for ever and ever. Amen.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By Silvanus, a faithful brother unto you, as I suppose, I have written briefly, exhorting, and testifying that this is the true grace of God wherein ye stand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "Acts 15:34 (32–34); 2 Cor. 1:19; 1 Thes. 1:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The church that is at Babylon, elected together with you, saluteth you; and so doth Marcus my son.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Babylon."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 18
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Greet ye one another with a kiss of charity. Peace be with you all that are in Christ Jesus. Amen.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
